The member copies are already as cheap as they can be. Nearly all the work here happens in `FieldBase`'s copy constructor, which this function cannot change. So the rewrite keeps the same initializer-list form, which the compiler turns into direct member copies, and expect no measurable speedup. Behavior is identical.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field),
      profile(field.profile),
      profileIndex(field.profileIndex),
      type(field.type),
      isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```